{"parents":[{"StatuteId":2048328,"Type":"Title","Statute":"23A"},{"StatuteId":2048517,"Type":"Chapter","Statute":"11"}],"Previous":"23A-10A-17","Next":"23A-11-1","StatuteId":2048517,"Statute":"23A-11","Type":"Chapter","CatchLine":"JOINDER FOR TRIAL ","FilePath":null,"FileName":null,"Htmlpath":null,"Htmlfilename":null,"Title":23,"TitleLetter":"A","Chapter":11,"ChapterLetter":null,"Section":0,"SubSec":0,"SubSection":null,"Word":null,"Html":"                                                                   \r\n                                                                          \r\n                                                                          \r\n                                                                          \r\n                                                                          \r\n<html>\r\n<head>\r\n<html>\r\n<head>\r\n<title>23A-11 JOINDER FOR TRIAL </title>\r\n<meta name=\"Keywords\" content=\"South Dakota Codified Laws SDCL 23A-11 JOINDER FOR TRIAL \">\r\n<meta name=\"Description\" content=\"South Dakota Codified Laws 23A-11\">\r\n</head>\r\n<body><div style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif'; font-size: 12pt; line-height: 1;\">\r\n\r\n<!-- File converted by Wp2Html Version 4.0  -->\r\n<!-- Email Andrew@brackenbeds.co.uk for more details  -->\r\n\r\n<!-- WP Style Open: System_34 --><!-- WP Style End: System_34 -->\r\n<div align=\"full\">\r\n<!-- WP Paired Style On: HG4 --><div align=\"center\"><!-- WP Style End: HG4 -->\r\nCHAPTER 23A-11\r\n<!-- WP Paired Style Off: HG4 --><!-- WP Style End: HG4 -->\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n<!-- WP Paired Style On: HG4C --><div align=\"center\"><!-- WP Style End: HG4C -->\r\nJOINDER FOR TRIAL\r\n<!-- WP Paired Style Off: HG4C --><!-- WP Style End: HG4C -->\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<br>\r\n<p>\r\n\r\n<!-- WP Paired Style On: B --><!-- WP Style End: B -->\r\n<a href=\"/statutes/DisplayStatute.aspx?Type=Statute&Statute=23A-11-1\">23A-11-1</a>\r\n<!-- WP Style Open: IN -->&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<!-- WP Style End: IN -->\r\n(Rule 13) Joinder for trial of indictments, informations, or defendants.\r\n<!-- WP Paired Style Off: B --><!-- WP Style End: B -->\r\n<br>\r\n<a href=\"/statutes/DisplayStatute.aspx?Type=Statute&Statute=23A-11-2\">23A-11-2</a>\r\n<!-- WP Style Open: IN -->&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<!-- WP Style End: IN -->\r\n(Rule 14) Relief from prejudicial joinder of offenses or defendants.<p>\r\n</p></div></div></body>\r\n</html>\r\n<hr><br><html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><head><meta charset=\"UTF-8\"><title></title><meta name=\"Generator\" content=\"PowerTools for Open XML\"><style>span { white-space: pre-wrap; }\r\np.s2048515Normal {\r\n    margin-top: 0;\r\n    margin-bottom: 0;\r\n    text-align: justify;\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    line-height: 108%;\r\n    margin-left: 0;\r\n    margin-right: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048515SENU {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048515CL {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\np.s2048515Normal-000000 {\r\n    margin-top: 0;\r\n    margin-bottom: 0;\r\n    text-indent: 0.50in;\r\n    text-align: justify;\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    line-height: 108%;\r\n    margin-left: 0;\r\n    margin-right: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048515DefaultParagraphFont {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048515000001 {\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048515SCL {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048515SCL-000002 {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\n</style></head><body><div style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif'; font-size: 12pt; line-height: 1;\"><div><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048515Normal\"><a href=\"https://sdlegislature.gov/Statutes/Codified_Laws/DisplayStatute.aspx?Type=Statute&amp;Statute=23A-11-1\"><span class=\"s2048515SENU\">23A-11-1</span></a><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2048515SENU\">. </span><span class=\"s2048515CL\">(Rule 13) Joinder for trial of indictments, informations, or defendants.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048515Normal-000000\"><span class=\"s2048515DefaultParagraphFont\">A court may order two or more indictments or informations, or both, to be tried together if the offenses, and the defendants, if there is more than one, could have been joined in a single indictment or information. The procedure shall be the same as if the prosecution were under a single indictment or information.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048515Normal\"><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2048515000001\"> </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048515Normal\"><span class=\"s2048515SCL\">Source:</span><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2048515SCL-000002\"><span>  Supreme Court Rule 395, 1939; SDC 1939 &amp; Supp 1960, § 34.3625; SDCL, § 23-42-4; <a rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"/api/SessionLaws/1978/178/null/null\" aria-label=\"SL 1978, ch 178\">SL 1978, ch 178</a>, § 129.</span></span></p></div></div></body></html><hr><br><html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><head><meta charset=\"UTF-8\"><title></title><meta name=\"Generator\" content=\"PowerTools for Open XML\"><style>span { white-space: pre-wrap; }\r\np.s2048516Normal {\r\n    margin-top: 0;\r\n    margin-bottom: 0;\r\n    text-align: justify;\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    line-height: 108%;\r\n    margin-left: 0;\r\n    margin-right: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048516SENU {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048516CL {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\np.s2048516Normal-000000 {\r\n    margin-top: 0;\r\n    margin-bottom: 0;\r\n    text-indent: 0.50in;\r\n    text-align: justify;\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    line-height: 108%;\r\n    margin-left: 0;\r\n    margin-right: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048516DefaultParagraphFont {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048516000001 {\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048516SCL {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048516SCL-000002 {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\n</style></head><body><div style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif'; font-size: 12pt; line-height: 1;\"><div><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048516Normal\"><a href=\"https://sdlegislature.gov/Statutes/Codified_Laws/DisplayStatute.aspx?Type=Statute&amp;Statute=23A-11-2\"><span class=\"s2048516SENU\">23A-11-2</span></a><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2048516SENU\">. </span><span class=\"s2048516CL\">(Rule 14) Relief from prejudicial joinder of offenses or defendants.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048516Normal-000000\"><span class=\"s2048516DefaultParagraphFont\">If it appears that a defendant or the state is prejudiced by a joinder of offenses or of defendants in an indictment or information or by such joinder for trial together, the court may order an election or separate trials of counts, grant a severance of defendants or provide whatever other relief justice requires. In ruling on a motion by a defendant for severance the court may order the prosecuting attorney to deliver to the court for inspection in camera any statements or confessions made by the defendants which the state intends to introduce in evidence at the trial.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048516Normal\"><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2048516000001\"> </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048516Normal\"><span class=\"s2048516SCL\">Source:</span><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2048516SCL-000002\"><span>  Supreme Court Rules 366, 395, 1939; SDC 1939 &amp; Supp 1960, §§ 34.3009, 34.3625; SDCL, §§ 23-32-8, 23-42-4; <a rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"/api/SessionLaws/1978/178/null/null\" aria-label=\"SL 1978, ch 178\">SL 1978, ch 178</a>, § 130.</span></span></p></div></div></body></html></head></html>","Credits":null,"StatuteText":null,"Article":null,"Created":null,"CreatedById":null,"LastUpdated":null,"LastUpdatedBy":null,"Repealed":false,"StatuteReferencesReferencesStatute":[],"StatuteReferencesStatute":[]}